1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Elling Clarence Ellingsen was born in Seattle on January 23, 1917 and died from cancer on December 8, 1977. He joined the Navy during WWII. He worked as a commercial fisherman along with his brother Parker and fath
2 CONC er Elling. Both the boys started fishing with their dad when they were 10 years old. His father owned the fishing vessel (F/V) ''Fremont''; he and Parker owned F/V ''National'' and Parker co-owned F/V ''Totem''. Later, Elling and 
2 CONC his wife Mildrid owned Smith Cove Oil Co. Elling's father was Elling Mathias Ellingson Nakken from Fiksdal, Norway, who immigrated to the US on July 28, 1906 aboard the ship ''Baltic''. He changed his last name to Ellingsen. He ma
2 CONC rried Klara (Clara) Elvine Standal, the youngest of three sisters from Aalesund, on Dec. 28, 1911. They had 5 children in six years (Lillian, Parker, Elling, Thelma, Irene). Elling's cousin was Gunnar Nakken, a well-known accordio
2 CONC nist from Fiksdal.
2 CONT      Mildrid was an excellent musician and music was always a huge part of her life. She played the organ for services at Vineland Lutheran Church in Poulsbo, Washington as a young girl and also played piano, accordion, Hawaiian g
2 CONC uitar and banjo. She played accordion with the Helga Melinder Orchestra during the war and provided beautiful dance music at many venues in Seattle and outlying areas. She had her own Ford and loved to travel. She had an adventure
2 CONC some spirit!
