1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Anna was the first of eight children born to Anders Misfjord and Anne Domaas. She was born in 1873, and raised on the Misfjord farm near Vestnes. Anna was given a middle name, Pauline. None of her sisters were so b
2 CONC lessed. At some point she met Rasmus Soraas who lived on one of the Soras farms just a short ways across Lake Flatevagen. Anna and Rasmus commited to a life together, but before marrying Rasmus went to America to earn money and ex
2 CONC plore a possible new life there. He went in 1893 at age twenty-one, and returned about seven years later. They were married in the “new” Vestnes church September 20, 1901. She was twenty-eight at the time and Rasmus was twenty-nin
2 CONC e. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Although Rasmus was the oldest of eight in his family he decided to move on rather than continue to farm at Soras. The farm was small and could only support one family. In 1902 they set off by boat to America with her brother Kris
2 CONC toffer and younger sister Anne. Anna was in the early stages of pregnancy with her son Harold during the voyage, and the ocean was rough. She was sick most of the voyage, and with that memory she never considered returning to her 
2 CONC home country by boat. 
2 CONT
2 CONT After landing in New York they traveled by train to Valley City, North Dakota where they settled. Rasmus bought a set of books and taught himself carpentry although he had developed some skills in Norway.  Rasmus built their home 
2 CONC and they lived there the rest of their lives. The climate was about the same as in Vestnes so they were comfortable. Because most of the people in Valley City spoke Norwegian she never had to learn to read or write English. Anna r
2 CONC aised three boys and two girls. All went to college and some had advanced degrees. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna was good natured and known for her pleasant personality. She was recognized for her needlework. Some of her work was shown at fairs in the area. They were charter members of Our Saviors Lutheran Church where services were hel
2 CONC d in Norwegian. On their 50th anniversary they were honored as the “oldest in membership in the church”.
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna was a very strong woman, when her last child Alpha was a baby Anna was in the hospital for three months to have a fast growing tumor removed. Alpha lived at the hospital during that time so she could be nursed.
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna passed away at the age of eighty-seven two years after Rasmus died. Since their marriage they had never been separated, and those last two years were difficult for her without Rasmus. 
