1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mildrid was an excellent musician and music was always a huge part of her life. She played the organ for services at Vineland Lutheran Church in Poulsbo, Washington as a young girl and also played piano, accordion,
2 CONC  Hawaiian guitar and banjo. She played accordion with the Helga Melinder Orchestra during the war and provided beautiful dance music at many venues in Seattle and outlying areas. She had her own Ford and loved to travel. She had a
2 CONC n adventuresome spirit! Her husband, Elling Clarence Ellingsen, was born in Seattle on January 23, 1917 and died from cancer on December 8, 1977. He joined the Navy during WWII. He worked as a commercial fisherman along with his b
2 CONC rother Parker and father Elling. Both the boys started fishing with their dad when they were 10 years old. His father owned the fishing vessel (F/V) ''Fremont''; he and Parker owned F/V ''National'' and Parker co-owned F/V ''Totem
2 CONC ''. Later, Elling and his wife Mildrid owned Smith Cove Oil Co., where she worked in the office and he drove oil truck. Elling's father was Elling Mathias Ellingson Nakken from Fiksdal, Norway, who immigrated to the US on July 28,
2 CONC  1906 aboard the ship ''Baltic''. He changed his last name to Ellingsen. He married Klara (Clara) Elvine Standal, the youngest of three sisters from Aalesund, on Dec. 28, 1911. They had 5 children in six years (Lillian, Parker, El
2 CONC ling, Thelma, Irene). Elling's cousin was Gunnar Nakken, a well-known accordionist from Fiksdal.
2 CONT
