1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 17. juni 1818 his son Johannes is born at Hitra prestegj. The boys father is mentioned as Jens Johannesen and his mother is Anna Marta Tollefsd. Lem. <br/>
2 CONT http://www.arkivverket.no/URN:kb_read?idx_kildeid=2373&idx_id=2373&uid=ny&idx_side=-10
2 CONT
2 CONT Jens Johansen and Anna Martha Tøllefsd. Are married 01.10.1813, in Kristiansund. Jens is from Hopsøen. Hopsjøen is a place on Hitra. <br/>
2 CONT Transcribed http://digitalarkivet.arkivverket.no/kb/vi/person/pv00000001544095<br/>
2 CONT Scanned http://www.arkivverket.no/URN:kb_read?idx_kildeid=2283&idx_id=2283&uid=ny&idx_side=-221
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna Martha is the daughter of Tollov Nicolai Lem and Maren Christina Pedersdatter Ruksæt. They had 2 daughters. Anne Marthe Tollovsdotter, born 14 March, baptized 25 March 1786 in Kristiansund<br/>
2 CONT http://www.arkivverket.no/URN:kb_read?idx_kildeid=2283&idx_id=2283&uid=ny&idx_side=-225 <br/>
2 CONT and Martha Tollevsdotter born 26 August, baptized 9 September 1787 in Kristiansund<br/>
2 CONT http://www.arkivverket.no/URN:kb_read?idx_kildeid=2283&idx_id=2283&uid=ny&idx_side=-225
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the Einar Thurn-Christensens archives the oldest daughter died as a young child we suppose that she is daughter # 2 and that she uses the name Anne.<br/>
2 CONT http://sedak.ikamr.no/2014/sed0060-etc/sed0060013/01/#109/z
2 CONT
2 CONT =The family Jens Johannesen and Anna Martha Tollefsdatter Lem=
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1813'''<br/>
2 CONT Johanna Nicolina born 09.06.1813 in Kristiansund, out of wedlock. Mother is Marta Tøllefsd. Lem. The parents married in November the same year.<br/>
2 CONT http://digitalarkivet.arkivverket.no/kb/dp/person/pd00000006722408<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1818'''<br/>
2 CONT As mentioned above Johan born on Hitra i 7. juni 1818
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1819'''<br/>
2 CONT Moving from Kristiansund to Hitra. Jens Johansen Hopsjøen, 33 år. Ane Martha Tollevsdatter Lem<br/>
2 CONT https://media.digitalarkivet.no/kb20070913620145
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1820'''<br/>
2 CONT Their son Jens is born 30.12.1820 in  Stadsbygd at the farm Selbekken, in Lensvik. The baptism is in Stadsbygd kirke 24. February 1821. The father is mention as Jens Johannesen Lem. The mother is Martha Tolløvsdatter. They live at
2 CONC  Selbekken.<br/>
2 CONT http://www.arkivverket.no/URN:kb_read?idx_kildeid=16167&idx_id=16167&uid=ny&idx_side=-22
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1823'''<br/>
2 CONT In 1823 a girl is born by the name of Ane Margrethe. The parents names are Jens Johnsen Landrø and Ane Martha Tønnesdatter.  This is probably mistakenly written for Tøllevdatter.<br/>
2 CONT https://media.digitalarkivet.no/kb20070905660210
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1825'''<br/>
2 CONT The daughter Berit Maria born 21 November 1825 in Stadsbygd. Parents are Jens Johannesen Landrøe and Ane Martha Tollofsdatter.<br/>
2 CONT http://www.arkivverket.no/URN:kb_read?idx_kildeid=16167&idx_id=16167&uid=ny&idx_side=-50
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1829'''<br/>
2 CONT The daughter Andrea born 20 May 1829 Stadsbygd (Landrøplass). Parents are Jens Johannesen and Ane Martha Tollovsdatter.<br/>
2 CONT http://www.arkivverket.no/URN:kb_read?idx_kildeid=16168&idx_id=16168&uid=ny&idx_side=-28
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1859'''
2 CONT Jens dies. 77 years old. Lived at Selbekk #. 27
2 CONT https://www.digitalarkivet.no/kb20050607020271
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1879'''
2 CONT Anne Martha dies 80 years old. # 8
2 CONT https://www.digitalarkivet.no/kb20070420620590
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT We find the family mentioned in ”Lensvikboka : spredte trekk fra bygda og folkets liv og virke til 1940” page 205, for the farm Landrø. There are reasons to believe that Seem is mistakenly written for Lem.. Translated it says<br/>
2 CONT '”In 1823 Jens Johansen Seem and wife Anne Martha Tellefsdatter moved to Landrøe. They had several children, amongst them Andrea Jensdatter, b. 1829, married with musician  Berg in Trondheim. The family moved later to Selbekkplass
2 CONC en and lived there for a while.”'<br/>
2 CONT https://www.nb.no/items/fe42ecffa4d28d879776a36062db15ba?page=207&searchText=Lensvikboka
2 CONT
2 CONT =Who was Jens Johannesen?=
2 CONT
2 CONT There are 4 candidates.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Candidate 1==
2 CONT '''We don't consider candidate 1 anymore as Jens Johannesen form Selbekks burial is found'''
2 CONT Jens Johannesen and his wife moved to Lensvik. We do find a Jens Johansen from Lensvik. He was 5 years old in the 1801 census. His father is Johan Haftorsen and mother Siri Poulsdatter.<br/>
2 CONT https://www.digitalarkivet.no/en/census/person/pf01058438000204
2 CONT
2 CONT Jens Johansen was born 17. August 1794. <br/>
2 CONT https://media.digitalarkivet.no/kb20070905650523
2 CONT
2 CONT There was a census done in 1815 at Stadsbygd.<br/>
2 CONT Here we find Jens Johannesen 20 years old on the farm Haarsager.<br/>
2 CONT https://media.digitalarkivet.no/ft20110314620099<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT The tax list from 1816 Johan Haftorsen son, Jens Johansen lives on the farm Haarsager<br/>
2 CONT https://media.digitalarkivet.no/kb20070905660086
2 CONT
2 CONT Jens Johansen died 43 years old, 13 July, buried  20 July 1837. He lived on the farm Haarsager<br/>
2 CONT https://media.digitalarkivet.no/kb20070905670040
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Candidate 2==
2 CONT
2 CONT In the 1801 census we find a Jens Johannessen who was 26 years old in 1801. He was a farmhand on the farm Hopsøen (Hopsjøen) at Hijra<br/>
2 CONT https://www.digitalarkivet.no/census/person/pf01058436001217
2 CONT
2 CONT He is probably the son of Johannes Schaaren, born 3. February 1771<br/>
2 CONT https://media.digitalarkivet.no/kb20070904700649<br/>
2 CONT We will mention that 2 of the witnesses are from Faxvaag.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Candidate 3==
2 CONT
2 CONT In the 1801 census we find a Johannessen 11 years old. He is a farm worker on the farm Valøen. Valøen is on the island of Dolmøya on Hijra.<br/>
2 CONT https://www.digitalarkivet.no/census/person/pf01058436001483
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Candidate 4==
2 CONT
2 CONT In a register of sailors at Trondheim, 1804 to 1809, there is a Jens Johannesen Lie from Bakland in Trondheim. e is registered born or baptized 3/8 1792. It is noted that he is the son of the late sailor Johannes Lie. In 1807 he w
2 CONC as stationed at Hitra.<br/>
2 CONT https://media.digitalarkivet.no/ru20100922630941
2 CONT
2 CONT One of these last two candidates are probably the Jens Johansen Hops;en that married Helvig Olsdatter Helsøe in 1811.<br/>
2 CONT https://media.digitalarkivet.no/kb20070905610102
2 CONT
2 CONT =Which Jens Johannesen was married to Anne Martha Tollevsdatter Lem?=
2 CONT
2 CONT Candidate 1 is not considered.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jens Johansen, son of Johan Schaaren, can be tied to Faxvaag through the witnesses at the baptism. Skåren is a neighboring farm to Faxvåg. He is 11 or 14 years older than Anne Marta. Arguments for this candidate are that he is fro
2 CONC m the area at Asmundvåg, Hitra where his first son is born and his wife is mentioned. His son Johannes moved later to Asmundvåg and he worked at Hopsjø in 1801.
2 CONT
2 CONT We know very little about Jens that lives on Valøya. In 1801 he is 11 years old and registered as a farm hand. Could he be a foster child? His age would fit being married to Helvig Olsdatter Helsøe in 1811. Except for his age ther
2 CONC e is little that points to that he is the right candidate.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the birth of Johanna Nicolina in 1813 it says that the father Jens Johannesen is a sailor. This would fit Jens from Trondheim. He could also be the foster boy from Valøya. The age would fit and the fact that he is orphaned.
2 CONT
2 CONT Candidate 1 from Lensvik doesn’t seem very likely. <br/>
2 CONT Though the ages of candidate 3 an 4 fit there is no data that links them to Anne Marta. <br/>
2 CONT At the moment it seems that Jens Johannessen from Schaaren/Asmundvåg is the correct candidate.
