1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Esther P. Larsen, 99, Casselton, ND, died on Sunday, May 8, 2005 in Bethany Homes, Fargo, ND.<BR />Esther was born to Rasmus and Anna Soroos in Valley City, ND on March 1, 1906. She graduated from Valley City State
2 CONC  Teachers College and taught school in Fessenden and Kindred, ND. She married Roger Larsen in Valley City in August of 1928. They were partners in the Larsen Department Store in Kindred until 1937, when they moved to Casselton and
2 CONC  opened the Federated Store which they operated until their retirement. In retirement they spent winters in Mesa, AZ and summers at the family lake cottage on Big Floyd Lake, MN.<BR />Esther was a long time member of Martin's Luth
2 CONC eran Church and Martin's Lutheran Ladies Aid. She was a Past Matron of Orient Chapter #16 of the Eastern Star in Casselton. <BR />Esther was an avid gardener both with outside flowers in the summer and a large selection of indoor 
2 CONC plants in the winter. She was a great follower of sports, starting with her own children and later with her grandchildren. She followed with great interest the Minnesota Twins, Minnesota Vikings, Chicago Bulls, golf and college sp
2 CONC orts. She never gave up until the game was over.<BR />She was preceded in death by her husband Roger who died in 1981, her parents, and three brothers and a sister.<BR />She entered Bethany Towers in 1994 and Bethany Nursing Home 
2 CONC in 2002.<BR />Esther is survived by sons, Donald, Casselton; Douglas (Sally) of Fargo; daughter Lynda (Joe) Dolejs of Burnsville, MN; eight grandchildren and 19 great grandchildren.<BR />Visitation: Wednesday from 6 to 7:30 in the
2 CONC  West Funeral Home chapel in Casselton, and one hour prior to the service in the church.<BR />Funeral: Thursday morning at 10:30 in Martins Lutheran Church in Casselton.<BR />Burial: Casselton Cemetery
