2 DATE ABT 1910
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Confirmation: https://www.digitalarkivet.no/view/279/pk00000001908687
2 CONT
2 CONT 1865 census for Einen, Vestnes:
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.digitalarkivet.no/en/census/person/pf01038291002474
2 CONT
2 CONT Out-migration record, 1879 (to Bergen):
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.digitalarkivet.no/en/view/291/pu00000000165548
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.werelate.org/wiki/Person:Thorbj%C3%B8rn_Husa_Hammeraas_(1)
2 CONT
2 CONT From ancestry.com:
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.ancestry.com/mediaui-viewer/tree/20456904/person/950199237/media/078b6646-cc1d-43c6-9465-d3a1dd1502b3  (Posted 19 Sep 2010 by TMB12)
2 CONT
2 CONT Torbjørn Rasmussen made his living as a Blacksmith. He also served as a Second carpenter on the Ship "Lehmkuhl" in the aprox year 1881. From what I could find out, Torbjorn was not married to Anna (Ingeborg's mother). I am not sur
2 CONC e if he was married to the unknown mother of Martha or if she was a full sister to Ingeborg. My great grandmother Ingeborg's obituary does indicate that she had brothers back in Norway but it does not name them or indicate whether
2 CONC  they are half or full brothers. What is documented is Torbjørn emigrated to USA, probably around 1900. I do not know where he settled, but he married and had at least three children: Rose, Thomas, and Carla. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife died after few years, and Torbjørn died in a railway accident few years later. His two eldest children were adopted by someone in USA. His daughter Carla was adopted by a couple from Germany and moved to Bremen Germany. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married a German naval officer, Helmuth von Mucke from Zwickau. During the war 1914 -18 he became a war "hero". Helmuth opposed Hitler when he became leader of the Nazi party. He was arrested several times, but survived. The H
2 CONC itler regime suspected Carla to be of Jewish descent. By the help of her Norwegian family she was able to prove she was of Norwegian, not Jewish, heritage, and survived.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had 5 children. A son died in Russia during the war, the others live in Germany and Netherlands. Carla and her son Bjørn visited Norway in 1959. Torbjorn's family in their own right can claim direct descent to royalty and som
2 CONC e of the most interesting characters of Norwegian descent.
